    "The retrieval score is not a probability.  It is a geometric score.  Later we may convert scores to a probability-like distribution using a softmax, but this adds modeling assumptions.\n",
    "\n",
    "## 19.9 Sparse retrieval with TF-IDF\n",
    "\n",
    "Dense retrieval is not always better than sparse retrieval.  If a query contains a precise course number, policy phrase, chemical name, theorem name, or error message, exact lexical matching can be essential.\n",
