    "\n",
    "## 19.28 Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "Retrieval-augmented generation combines language modeling with search.  The retrieval part is fundamentally geometric: map queries and chunks to vectors, compute similarities, and return top-ranked evidence.  The generation part is probabilistic: condition a language model on the query and retrieved context.\n",
